        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joe Orton, Bernard-Marie Koltès, The Beatles\n- Works: Up Against It, La Nuit juste avant les Forêts, Sallinger, Dans la Solitude des Champs de Coton\n- Roles: playwright, author, theatre director\n\nFacts:\n- Joe Orton was born on 1 January 1933 and died on 9 August 1967.\n- Joe Orton was an English playwright and author.\n- Bernard-Marie Koltès was born on 9 April 1948 and died on 15 April 1989.\n- Bernard-Marie Koltès was a French playwright and theatre director.\n- Bernard-Marie Koltès was best known for the plays La Nuit juste avant les Forêts (1976), Sallinger (1977), and Dans la Solitude des Champs de Coton (1986).\n- Joe Orton wrote Up Against It in 1967 as an unproduced script for The Beatles.\n- Up Against It was written for The Beatles at the height of their fame.",
